 "divergences": [
  {
   "citation": "Teranode's freeze path has no hold state by design: the alert service freezes the output in the UTXO store and a block spending it is refused at the store's spend (stores/utxo/aerospike/spend.go:1103-1107), its best header chosen among blocks not marked invalid (stores/blockchain/sql/GetBestBlockHeader.go:134-135) [SRC]. The reference holds such a block out of its best chain for -softconsensusfreezeduration blocks (a setting, default 3, src/validation.h:219; the trigger src/validation.cpp:3402-3406; the hold src/block_index.h:283-285) [SRC] and then activates through it. The chain decision differs on the same blocks once the hold lapses",
   "class": "chain-split",
   "detail": "consensus, #153",
   "id": "soft-freeze-hold-lapse",
   "key": "list:soft-freeze-hold-lapse",
   "reference": "the leg's row, named: tl.soft-freeze (during the hold): docs/records/20261016-173411-s8-140-soft-freeze-reference-s3.json (ns-140, #140; the row measured on both oracles (the ledger's `tl.soft-freeze` `measured`)); row c (after the reference's hold lapses): docs/records/20261017-170959-s4b-94-teranode-alert-path-s4b.md (hz-94, #94; 8 rows: 3 agree, 3 differ, 2 not run (the signed-alert gossip delivery, go-alert-system v0.1.17's drop))",
   "reference_record": "",
   "row": "soft-freeze",
   "row_kind": "chain-split",
   "ruling": "docs/PLAN-2026-10-05-SPEC-ALONE.md section 6, S8's divergences ruled 2026-10-17 (card Z8, `94: issues`): the chain-split row, issue #153",
   "source": "the obligation list",
   "teranode": "the same leg's row (its record withheld by name; the counts are the public ones)"
  },
  {
   "citation": "A node built as many services across many machines takes the operator's invalidate from one signed channel, the alert service (services/alert/node.go:160-176 InvalidateBlock; the keys settings/settings.go:198,202) [SRC], beside its RPC handler (services/rpc/handlers.go:1862, #85's contract); the reference takes it from the RPC credential's holder (src/rpc/blockchain.cpp:2732-2768) [SRC]. The authority is a node setting (docs/PARAMETERS.md section 8.10); the action is the same whichever authority admits it",
   "class": "design",
   "detail": "policy, #154",
   "id": "alert-invalidate",
   "key": "list:alert-invalidate",
   "reference": "the leg's row, named: row e: docs/records/20261017-170959-s4b-94-teranode-alert-path-s4b.md (hz-94, #94; 8 rows: 3 agree, 3 differ, 2 not run (the signed-alert gossip delivery, go-alert-system v0.1.17's drop))",
   "reference_record": "",
   "row": "alert-system",
   "row_kind": "design",
   "ruling": "docs/PLAN-2026-10-05-SPEC-ALONE.md section 6, S8's divergences ruled 2026-10-17 (card Z8, `94: issues`): a design row, issue #154",
   "source": "the obligation list",
   "teranode": "the same leg's row (its record withheld by name; the counts are the public ones)"
  },
  {
   "citation": "The peer ban arrives at Teranode by the same signed channel (services/alert/node.go:189-216 BanPeer), beside its RPC handler (`setban`, services/rpc/handlers.go:2447, mapped at services/rpc/Server.go:208) [SRC]; the reference bans by RPC (`setban`, `src/rpc/net.cpp:669-757` at `6504a3af`) [SRC]. The authority is a node setting (docs/PARAMETERS.md section 8.10); the trust root changes who, never what (`trust_root_changes_who_not_what`), but the ban's length differs: 100 years by the alert against the reference's `-bantime`, a day by default (`ban_until_differs`), and the reference's ban only lengthens where Teranode's overwrites",
   "class": "design",
   "detail": "policy, #154",
   "id": "alert-ban",
   "key": "list:alert-ban",
   "reference": "the leg's row, named: row f: docs/records/20261017-170959-s4b-94-teranode-alert-path-s4b.md (hz-94, #94; 8 rows: 3 agree, 3 differ, 2 not run (the signed-alert gossip delivery, go-alert-system v0.1.17's drop))",
   "reference_record": "",
   "row": "alert-system",
   "row_kind": "design",
   "ruling": "docs/PLAN-2026-10-05-SPEC-ALONE.md section 6, S8's divergences ruled 2026-10-17 (card Z8, `94: issues`): a design row, issue #154",
   "source": "the obligation list",
   "teranode": "the same leg's row (its record withheld by name; the counts are the public ones)"
  },
  {
   "citation": "Teranode's alert service confiscates by reassignment: a frozen output is given a new locking script (stores/utxo/aerospike/alert_system.go:233-270 ReAssignUTXO, teranode.lua:870-958) and stays unspendable for utxostore_reassignedUtxoSpendableAfterBlocks blocks (a node setting, default 1000, settings/settings.go:528; docs/PARAMETERS.md section 8.10) [SRC]; the reference has no reassign and confiscates by a whitelisted confiscation transaction instead (#70; the row rl.alert-service)",
   "class": "design",
   "detail": "policy, #94",
   "id": "alert-reassign",
   "key": "list:alert-reassign",
   "reference": "the leg's row, named: the reassign row: docs/records/20261017-203139-s4b-94-teranode-store-half-s4b.md (hz-94s, #94; 8 rows run: agree 6, differ 2; and 1 row not run by name (the alert gossip delivery), the #94 comment's counts)",
   "reference_record": "",
   "row": "alert-system",
   "row_kind": "design",
   "ruling": "docs/PLAN-2026-10-05-SPEC-ALONE.md section 6, the same entry: classified design by lane close-88 under card Z8's framing rule, the class the owner's to confirm at #88's close",
